@startuml
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
left to right direction

actor "Administrators / Operators" as Admin
actor "API Clients" as ApiClient
actor "AWS CloudFormation (Deployment)" as CFN

node "AWS Account / Region" as AWS {
  node "Web Management Console\n(Hosted & Distributed)" as WebConsole
  component "Identity & Auth Service\n(e.g., Cognito / OIDC)" as IdP

  component "Amazon API Gateway\nREST API (Stage: prod, Type: REGIONAL)" as APIGW
  component "AWS Lambda\nAPI Backend" as LambdaAPI

  component "AWS Step Functions\nSimulation Orchestrator" as Orchestrator
  component "AWS Lambda\nRoute Loader" as RouteLoader
  component "AWS Lambda\nDevice Simulator Worker" as SimWorker

  database "Amazon DynamoDB\nTables: Simulations, DeviceTypes" as DDB
  folder "Amazon S3\nROUTE_BUCKET" as S3
  cloud "AWS IoT Core\nIoT Topics" as IoT

  queue "Amazon CloudWatch Logs\nAPI Access Logs (JSON)" as Logs
  component "AWS X-Ray\nTracing Enabled" as XRay

  component "AWS Lambda\nCustom Resource Handler" as CfnHandler
}

' End-user and client access
Admin --> WebConsole
WebConsole --> IdP : Authenticate
WebConsole --> APIGW : HTTPS (CORS)
ApiClient --> APIGW : HTTPS
APIGW ..> IdP : Authorize requests

' API layer and integrations
APIGW --> LambdaAPI : Lambda proxy integration
APIGW --> Logs : Access logs (JSON, INFO)
APIGW --> XRay : Traces

' Backend services and data stores
LambdaAPI --> DDB : Manage simulations & device types
LambdaAPI --> Orchestrator : Start simulation

' Simulation workflow
Orchestrator --> RouteLoader : Task: Load route state
RouteLoader --> S3 : Get route JSON\n(key = routeName or route-{id}.json)
Orchestrator --> SimWorker : Task: Execute simulation
SimWorker --> IoT : Publish simulated messages

' Deployment-time custom resource
CFN --> CfnHandler : Invoke custom resource
CfnHandler --> CFN : Construct & send response body

' Notes capturing key requirements and constraints
note right of APIGW
- Methods: GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, OPTIONS
- CORS preflight enabled (200)
- Allowed headers:
  Authorization, Content-Type,
  X-Amz-Date, X-Amz-Security-Token, X-Api-Key
- Request validation: parameters & body
- Endpoint Type: REGIONAL
- Tracing enabled
end note

note right of Logs
API access logging:
- JSON format with standard fields
- Method logging level: INFO
end note

note right of RouteLoader
Route loading from S3:
- Bucket: ROUTE_BUCKET
- Reads UTF-8 JSON object
- Uses routeInfo.routeName as key, or
  generates default: route-{randomId}.json
- Assembles route state:
  routeName, odometer, routeStage,
  burndown, burndownCalc, routeEnded,
  route, randomTriggers
- Error propagated on S3 retrieval failure
end note

note right of IoT
Simulated device messages
published to AWS IoT topics
end note
@enduml
